JENKINS INSTALLATION USING DOCKER 

1.  docker –version
    -   Verifies that Docker is installed and displays its version.
2.  sudo systemctl enable docker
    -   Enables Docker service to start automatically at system boot.
3.  sudo systemctl start docker
    -   Starts the Docker service immediately.
4.  sudo docker pull jenkins/jenkins:lts
    -   Downloads the official Jenkins LTS Docker image from Docker Hub.
5.  sudo docker images
    -   Lists all Docker images available on the system to verify
        Jenkins image.
6.  sudo docker run -d –name jenkins -p 8080:8080 -p 50000:50000
    jenkins/jenkins:lts
    -   Creates and runs a Jenkins container in detached mode with
        required ports exposed.
7.  sudo docker ps
    -   Displays running Docker containers to confirm Jenkins is active.
8.  sudo docker exec jenkins cat
    /var/jenkins_home/secrets/initialAdminPassword
    -   Retrieves the initial admin password generated by Jenkins.
9.  ip a
    -   Displays the system IP address to access Jenkins from a browser.
10. sudo docker ps
    -   Final verification to ensure Jenkins container is running
        properly.
11. sudo docker stop jenkins
    -   Stops the currently running Jenkins container safely.
12. sudo docker rm -f jenkins
    -   Removes the existing Jenkins container to recreate it with
        volume support.
13. sudo docker volume create jenkins_home
    -   Creates a Docker volume to store Jenkins data persistently.
14. sudo docker volume ls
    -   Lists available Docker volumes to verify jenkins_home is
        created.
15. sudo docker run -d –name jenkins -p 8080:8080 -p 50000:50000 -v
    jenkins_home:/var/jenkins_home jenkins/jenkins:lts
    -   Runs Jenkins container with persistent storage mounted to
        /var/jenkins_home.
16. sudo docker ps
    -   Confirms that the Jenkins container is running with exposed
        ports.
17. sudo docker exec jenkins cat
    /var/jenkins_home/secrets/initialAdminPassword
    -   Retrieves the new initial admin password after volume-based
        setup.
18. sudo docker volume inspect jenkins_home
    -   Displays volume details and mount location to confirm persistent
        storage path.
